# Git commit identity

When creating commits in this repository, always use:

- **Email:** `pvjthomas@users.noreply.github.com`
- **Name:** `pvjthomas`

This avoids GitHub push rejections from private email privacy settings (GH007).

For commits made via the agent, set author and committer explicitly if needed:

```bash
GIT_AUTHOR_NAME="pvjthomas" \
GIT_AUTHOR_EMAIL="pvjthomas@users.noreply.github.com" \
GIT_COMMITTER_NAME="pvjthomas" \
GIT_COMMITTER_EMAIL="pvjthomas@users.noreply.github.com" \
git commit -m "message"
```

Do not use personal emails (e.g. `@gmail.com`) in commits for this repo.
